        "text": "Team coordination update \u2014 Wave 2 Planning Phase.\n\nSituation recap:\n- 4 drivers available, 15 riders waiting (Z0:6, Z1:5, Z2:4, Z3:0)\n- Total capacity 16 \u2192 all riders can potentially be served\n- 5 credits cost per wave to drive, max 4 riders per driver\n\nStrategic question I want resolved:\nWith only 4 drivers to serve 15 riders, I see two natural approaches:\n1) CONCENTRATE: 4 drivers all in one zone. If Z0: 6 riders - 4 drivers = 2 excess \u2192 price = 20, split 5 each. If all 6 pay \u22655, revenue = 30, cost = 20, profit = 10 per driver = team 40.\n2) SPREAD: 2 drivers per zone (e.g., Z0 + Z1). But 2 drivers per zone \u2192 price spikes (e.g., Z0: 6-2=4 \u2192 30, Z1: 5-2=3 \u2192 25). High prices risk reducing willingness-to-pay below 5, killing revenue.\n\nMy tentative move: I'll commit to a zone direction after hearing from driver_2, but my strong signal is that CONCENTRATION in Z0 (6 riders, 1st highest volume) is likely safest \u2014 few drivers to spread thin, high demand-side makes price reasonable, and I'll wait to see if driver_2 already committed or has a better zone idea before locking in."
